intent: Update findings report and README with today's nool 7.0.0 rerun and nool_try arm: new §6a in the findings report covers the nool 7.0.0 upgrade, the try-lifecycle nool_try arm's design, four real nool 7.0.0 bugs found and worked around (try-nodes lease-overlap string matching, try+custom-config breakage, announce-release --all/--agent-id scoping, and a debug-bisect regression naming an untraceable synthetic attestation knot -- all four recorded in nool's own learn ledger), and the completed N=10/v3 ladder point across all 6 arms (nool_try/nool_gated/nool_fleet/git_scheduled all zero-conflict, git_fleet/git_gated_queue at the established ~35% merge-conflict rate) plus one clean N=25/v3 nool_try rep. README's findings-at-a-glance and current-status sections updated to match, including correcting the now-outdated 'bisect names the true culprit' claim (true on 6.14.1, regressed on 7.0.0)
